From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel Arto <manuel.arto@nethermind.io>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:30:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(daisugi): carry the EIP-8288 starkProof of the
 current Nethermind format

The execution client now derives the header commitment from the proof bytes
and the payload's frame transactions, so the payload carries a single
starkProof (empty for blocks without dependencies) and no deps hash.
Lighthouse cannot recompute that commitment, so its optimistic-sync
block-hash check defers to the execution client for Daisugi payloads.
Removes the unused experimental aggregate payload containers.
